===Etymology===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*soː||[[I]]; [[me]]}}. Cognate with {{cog|thm|โซว}}.

There are 1st person single pronouns in Northern Austroasiatic branches with back vocalism and null-initial such as {{ncog|zng|ʔuː⁴}}, {{cog|kjg|-}} [Cuang] ''ʔoʔ'', {{cog|ril|-}} [Sak] ''ʔoʔ¹'', {{cog|pbv|o}}. However, the only case of competing {{IPAfont|*s-}} vs. null-onset in Vietic is {{ncog|mkh-vie-pro|*suh}} ~ {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*ʔuh||nest}}, which gave rise to {{ncog|vi|tổ}} and {{m|vi|ổ}} respectively.

